{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1136","id":4810914804,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABHsC79A","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1136","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1136.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1136.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/1136","number":1136,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add audited fixed-area squared-pole bound for Problem 2307037","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Accepted full affirmative mathematical deduction for Baernstein's question, Hayman–Lingham Problem7.37 (2307037 / AMR-022-7037).\n\nPublished preprint: **[10.5281/zenodo.23443039](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23443039)**. [Zenodo record and downloads](https://zenodo.org/records/23443039) contain the four-page note and source/verification archive. Alec Kriebel, ORCID0009-0001-9320-500X; version1.0.0,17October2026; CC BY4.0.\n\nFor every finite sum g(z)=sum lambda_j/(z-z_j)^2 with positive weights summing to one and arbitrary, possibly repeated, complex poles, there is ONE compact S(g) of exact area pi, independent of R, with ordinary finite integral over D_R outside S(g) at most2*pi*log(R)+pi*(log(2)+1/e) for EVERY real R>1. The leading2*pi is sharp; the additive constant is not claimed optimal. The quadrature identity is justified on all complement components, including holes. Parent and three distinct mathematical families reconstructed the original target and proof; all twelve original source artifacts remain unchanged.\n\nThe note explicitly credits the established Eremenko–Hamilton1995 indicator estimate and Levine–Peres2009 quadrature/smash-sum construction, with their antecedents. The2002 EH correction to the general-distortion coefficient does not affect the retained conformal-on-E theorem used for the indicator input; an independent supplement reproduces that dependency. No new singular-integral theorem, quadrature existence/regularity or general balayage/operator principle is claimed. Related Yongxi Lin and André Guerra work receives credit.\n\n**Priority limits:** No verified pre-PR explicit full-target answer was identified in the extensive bounded audit. This is not historical novelty, worldwide first discovery/publication or global-openness certification. Leung preliminary reports titled On a fixed area problem were located in AMS Abstracts11(1990)p181 and13(1992)p440, but their mathematical text was inaccessible; relevance remains unresolved. Other unavailable full/final bodies and exact read scopes are documented. Generic ingredients were logically available by2009; a newly supplied target-specific deduction is distinguished from an earlier recorded solution. Git dates do not certify historical public visibility or causal independence. [Full priority decision](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/84fc3dba426f9b2619b491980a8c060916a14045/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1136_2307037/ROOT_PRIORITY_DECISION.md).\n\nTwo successive fresh complete-package adversarial reviews passed the identical release with no unresolved issues: [package_01](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/84fc3dba426f9b2619b491980a8c060916a14045/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1136_2307037/reviews/package_01/REPORT.md), [package_02](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/84fc3dba426f9b2619b491980a8c060916a14045/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1136_2307037/reviews/package_02/REPORT.md). The portable runner checks all118 frozen authored audit members and twelve inputs; three offline mathematical programs pass ordinary/optimized modes with complete-output comparison, stated floating-diagnostic roundoff and four actual corrupted-oracle failures. The fourth source-bound target program also passes8totalruns/10actualfailures with a hash-pinned primary PDF, reproducible through explicit optional download in a disposable mirror. Frozen source archive rebuilds exactly from extraction under the same runtime. Floating calculations supplement universal written proof; no validated numerical/formal proof certificate is claimed.\n\nAI tools were used extensively in proof development, computation, adversarial verification, literature research and writing. These materials are **unrefereed** and have not undergone external human peer review or journal acceptance. No human outreach was prepared or initiated.\n\nProduction readback verified the exact reviewed file bytes and supplied metadata under the repository tool’s strict comparison rules. Zenodo changed only the description’s curly apostrophe to an ASCII apostrophe, a narrowly documented server representation normalization; all other supplied fields/content match. The frozen kit and metadata files remain unchanged. Google Workspace CLI added one DOI row at `'Math Puzzles'!A162:D162` and read it back exactly. Reviewed source head:`cbbe7826cca914588018c840ba99c6b7a59fa7f5`. PDF SHA256:`62c27c2a54e11d310cc600435576494fee15ce8ea30b7d9aef97736797cd4719`; source/verification ZIP SHA256:`b937a403bce56ab42fe8ba07b1df0f8e452f65addf4a74273fbce2c784da53df`.\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T11:38:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T22:36:58Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b622970753a43f0d0d2fd4983004fcb9513c4df8","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1136/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1136/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/1136/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/cbbe7826cca914588018c840ba99c6b7a59fa7f5","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:research/squared-pole-2307037-audited-bound","ref":"research/squared-pole-2307037-audited-bound","sha":"cbbe7826cca914588018c840ba99c6b7a59fa7f5","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":130771